# Local secrets for `wrangler pages dev` (copy to .dev.vars, which is gitignored).
# These mirror the Pages secrets set in production via `wrangler pages secret put`.

# Model keys. inference.config.json names which env var each feature's provider reads; the three
# below are the defaults. Add e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY here if you point a feature at OpenAI. See
# INFERENCE.md. Keys go here or in Pages secrets, never in inference.config.json.
#
# The chat/persona/extract/treatment pool. The route itself is session-gated (hd_session).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# /api/vault (W6): the vault-write bearer allowlist (`npm run allowlist` output). This is the
# last consumer of that script — it shared a value with CHAT_TOKEN until that secret was deleted.
VAULT_TOKEN=<comma-joined hashes from `npm run allowlist`>

# Session cookies (W44 P2): HMAC-SHA256 signing key for functions/_lib/session.ts.
# Set a long random value via `wrangler pages secret put SESSION_SECRET` — never commit
# a real value here.
SESSION_SECRET=<random-string>

# Passkey auth (W44 P3): WebAuthn relying-party identity for functions/_lib/webauthn.ts.
# RP_ID must be the bare domain (no scheme/port) the passkey is scoped to; ORIGIN must be the
# exact scheme+host(+port) the browser sends. Local dev values match `wrangler pages dev`'s
# default port below. Prod sets the real domain/origin via `wrangler pages secret put` (or vars,
# since these aren't secret) — never point RP_ID/ORIGIN at a dev value in a deployed environment.
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=localhost
WEBAUTHN_RP_NAME=LexiTar
WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8788

# Provider Finding refresh (W15/3b): a DISTINCT key so the money-spending Finding regeneration
# can't exhaust the chat key's budget. Unset, it falls back to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
FINDING_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Provider authorization token (W15/3b): the distinct secret handed to a proven clinician that
# authorizes /api/refresh-finding (functions/api/provider-token.ts, log.ts, logs.ts). Rotates
# independently of the vault/chat tokens. Also gates /api/refresh-range (M59).
PROVIDER_TOKEN=<random-string>

# Ranges, document-extract and leaf-regen (M59/Phase 2): a DISTINCT key so they can't exhaust the
# Finding/chat keys' budget. Unset, it falls back to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
RANGES_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Google OAuth (W45 §J). Provision a Web OAuth client in Google Cloud console; authorized redirect
# URI must be <host>/api/auth/google/callback. GOOGLE_KEK is the SERVER-HELD key-encryption key that
# wraps Google accounts' private keys (base64 of >=32 random bytes) — set it via
# `wrangler pages secret put GOOGLE_KEK`; losing/rotating it locks every Google-only account out.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<from Google Cloud console>
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<from Google Cloud console>
# GOOGLE_KEK=<base64 of 32 random bytes, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`>

# Error reporting (functions/api/client-error.ts and functions/api/_middleware.ts): uncaught browser
# errors and uncaught Function errors both become GitHub issues in this repo, one per fingerprint. Fine-grained PAT scoped to that one repo, Issues:
# read/write only. Unset → reports go to `wrangler pages deployment tail` only.
# CLIENT_ERROR_GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...
# CLIENT_ERROR_GITHUB_REPO=owner/name

# Support-access notice mail (functions/_lib/email.ts). Gmail API through a Google Cloud service
# account with domain-wide delegation, which signs a JWT impersonating GMAIL_SENDER — so the
# service account is the identity and the sender is the mailbox it is delegated to act as.
# GMAIL_SA_PRIVATE_KEY is the PKCS8 PEM out of the service-account JSON and may carry literal `\n`
# rather than real newlines (:13). Unset, a support grant is still recorded and still audited and
# `sendEmail` logs `[email] not sent — Gmail unconfigured` (:101-105) — the only thing lost is the
# patient being told it happened, which is why this group is optional in dev and not in prod.
# GMAIL_SA_CLIENT_EMAIL=<name>@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# GMAIL_SA_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n
# GMAIL_SENDER=noreply@<your-domain>
#
# EMAIL_FROM is DELIBERATELY not a line above. It is optional and defaults to
# `TinyTars <GMAIL_SENDER>` at functions/_lib/email.ts:107, so a template line would read as
# something you must fill in. Set it only to override the display From; the three names above are
# what the mail actually needs.

# Read-aloud (/api/speak). Azure Cognitive Services Speech. REGION is the short region id, which
# becomes the hostname at functions/api/speak.ts:40 (`<region>.tts.speech.microsoft.com`) — not a
# URL, not an endpoint. Unset, /api/speak answers 503 `not_configured` (:37) and nothing else is
# affected.
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=<Azure portal → your Speech resource → Keys and Endpoint>
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=eastus

# NOTE: the DB (D1), VAULT (R2), ASSETS (static) bindings and STORE_PREFIX var come from
# wrangler.jsonc — NOT from .dev.vars. Only secrets belong here.
